[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2672227783","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103084#issuecomment-2672227783","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103084","id":2672227783,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fRvXH","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-20T17:43:10Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T17:44:35Z","body":"Testing on Windows 11 with both `4.4.beta4`, `4.3.stable`, and `4.2.2.stable` and the result is the same, with brackets, so cannot replicate that this has changed, but I'd say this is the proper format and how these IDs are formatted on Windows in general, it's used in other places in the same way\n\nBut I can't replicate that this behaves differently in 4.4 and 4.3 as reported","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2672227783/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675545298","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103084#issuecomment-2675545298","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103084","id":2675545298,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6feZTS","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-21T21:08:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-21T21:08:19Z","body":"There's no specific format to this value, it depends on platform. In case of Windows it's returning [hardware profile GUID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winbase/ns-winbase-hw_profile_infoa), which is documented to have `{}`.\n\n> szHwProfileGuid[HW_PROFILE_GUIDLEN]\n>\n>The globally unique identifier (GUID) string for the current hardware profile. The string returned by [GetCurrentHwProfile](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/desktop/api/winbase/nf-winbase-getcurrenthwprofilea) encloses the GUID in curly braces, {}; for example:\n>\n> {12340001-4980-1920-6788-123456789012}","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675545298/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675549827","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103084#issuecomment-2675549827","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103084","id":2675549827,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6feaaD","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-21T21:11:17Z","updated_at":"2025-02-21T21:11:17Z","body":"Since the value itself is pretty meaningless, we probably can hash it and return it in the same format on all platforms.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675549827/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686048621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103084#issuecomment-2686048621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103084","id":2686048621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gGdlt","user":{"login":"SundaePixel","id":74124581,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MTI0NTgx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74124581?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel","html_url":"https://github.com/SundaePixel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T19:52:51Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T19:52:51Z","body":"> Since the value itself is pretty meaningless, we probably can hash it and return it in the same format on all platforms.\n\nIt's not entirely meaningless for the people that use it for file encryption or any other purpose of verification","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686048621/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686074698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103084#issuecomment-2686074698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103084","id":2686074698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gGj9K","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T20:05:31Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T20:05:51Z","body":"> for the people that use it for file encryption or any other purpose of verification\n\nYou should not use it for any persistent data or identification. Hardware ID can change if you change hardware (even if something simple like plunging the laptop to the docking station, or connecting eGPU), and it's easy to change it manually. It's only good for saving local user setting for specific hardware config.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686074698/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686169504","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103084#issuecomment-2686169504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103084","id":2686169504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gG7Gg","user":{"login":"SundaePixel","id":74124581,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MTI0NTgx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74124581?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel","html_url":"https://github.com/SundaePixel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T20:52:54Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T20:52:54Z","body":"> > for the people that use it for file encryption or any other purpose of verification\n> \n> You should not use it for any persistent data or identification. Hardware ID can change if you change hardware (even if something simple like plunging the laptop to the docking station, or connecting eGPU), and it's easy to change it manually. It's only good for saving local user setting for specific hardware config.\n\nNonetheless, regardless of the intended use, converting from Godot 4.3 to 4.4 will result in errors.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686169504/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686202667","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103084#issuecomment-2686202667","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103084","id":2686202667,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gHDMr","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T21:09:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T21:10:28Z","body":"Please provide more details, the results in my testing is identical between 4.3 and 4.4, the implementation for fetching this value *hasn't changed* between 4.3 and 4.4, it's the exact same code, and it just fetches the value from the OS, so the only way this could have changed between you running in 4.3 and you running in 4.4 would be if Windows itself changed\n\nDid you try it again with 4.3 now?\n\nThe code in 4.3:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/77dcf97d82cbfe4e4615475fa52ca03da645dbd8/platform/windows/os_windows.cpp#L1818-L1822\n\nThe code in 4.4:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/3ef055fecb16714760a1b7fdaf8b8f8f0a06114d/platform/windows/os_windows.cpp#L2239-L2243","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686202667/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686279160","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103084#issuecomment-2686279160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103084","id":2686279160,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gHV34","user":{"login":"SundaePixel","id":74124581,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MTI0NTgx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74124581?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel","html_url":"https://github.com/SundaePixel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SundaePixel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T21:48:49Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T21:48:49Z","body":"> Please provide more details, the results in my testing is identical between 4.3 and 4.4, the implementation for fetching this value _hasn't changed_ between 4.3 and 4.4, it's the exact same code, and it just fetches the value from the OS, so the only way this could have changed between you running in 4.3 and you running in 4.4 would be if Windows itself changed\n> \n> Did you try it again with 4.3 now?\n> \n> The code in 4.3:\n> \n> [godot/platform/windows/os_windows.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/77dcf97d82cbfe4e4615475fa52ca03da645dbd8/platform/windows/os_windows.cpp#L1818-L1822)\n> \n> Lines 1818 to 1822 in [77dcf97](/godotengine/godot/commit/77dcf97d82cbfe4e4615475fa52ca03da645dbd8)\n> \n>  String OS_Windows::get_unique_id() const { \n>  \tHW_PROFILE_INFOA HwProfInfo; \n>  \tERR_FAIL_COND_V(!GetCurrentHwProfileA(&HwProfInfo), \"\"); \n>  \treturn String((HwProfInfo.szHwProfileGuid), HW_PROFILE_GUIDLEN); \n>  } \n> The code in 4.4:\n> \n> [godot/platform/windows/os_windows.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/3ef055fecb16714760a1b7fdaf8b8f8f0a06114d/platform/windows/os_windows.cpp#L2239-L2243)\n> \n> Lines 2239 to 2243 in [3ef055f](/godotengine/godot/commit/3ef055fecb16714760a1b7fdaf8b8f8f0a06114d)\n> \n>  String OS_Windows::get_unique_id() const { \n>  \tHW_PROFILE_INFOA HwProfInfo; \n>  \tERR_FAIL_COND_V(!GetCurrentHwProfileA(&HwProfInfo), \"\"); \n>  \treturn String((HwProfInfo.szHwProfileGuid), HW_PROFILE_GUIDLEN); \n>  }\n\nThat's a good point, and when i went back into Godot 4.3 and tried to print it, it seems to be also encapsulated in {}. No idea what happened when i switched to 4.3 to 4.4. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686279160/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]